{"Debug error-level logs in production - Six r.log.Error() calls are used for routine operational messages like 'Annotations to clean by time' and 'cleaned annotations by time', not actual error conditions, which will flood error-level logs, trigger alerting systems, and dump potentially large ID arrays into log entries": 0.9757979512214661, "Batch loop stops early - untilDoneOrCancelled terminates when affected == 0, but with split SELECT+DELETE sessions, a concurrent cleaner can delete the fetched IDs first, causing affected==0 and premature termination even if more rows still match the condition": 0.6041254997253418, "Cleanup interval reduced 10x accidentally - The cleanup service ticker was changed from time.Minute * 10 to time.Minute * 1, increasing database cleanup load by 10x, and the existing 9-minute timeout in clean() means up to 9 overlapping cleanup operations can run concurrently": 0.9714028835296631, "O(n^2) memory allocations for SQLite - The SQLite fallback loop builds a single SQL query string by iteratively concatenating string parts for each ID, causing O(N^2) memory allocations for large batch sizes which can spike memory consumption by several gigabytes and potentially cause an OOM": 0.8843511939048767, "Very heavy integration test - The new integration test case inserts 40,003 annotations and 80,006 tags, which can be slow and memory-intensive for non-short test runs and can hurt developer experience": 0.5853312611579895}